fix(ci): unblock Bundle Size Gate by bypassing SEO build gate

Original task (#941): the GitHub Actions "Bundle Size Gate" job was
failing on every recent PR (#22) and on every push to main (#26-#28),
even though Vercel deploys were green.

Root cause
----------
The build dies inside the `seo-validate` Vite plugin
(`easy-locs-ea1eb0ed/vite-plugin-seo-validate.ts`, closeBundle hook).
Current main has ~10,400 prerendered pages whose meta description
exceeds 155 chars, so the plugin throws:

  [seo-validate] BUILD GATE: 10426 critical SEO issue(s) detected
  (threshold 0)

`vite build` exits 1 before `dist/assets` is ever written, so
`npm run bundle:gate` fails with no useful signal. Vercel deploys
succeed because the same plugin auto-bypasses when `VERCEL=1` is set
in the environment — GitHub Actions has no such variable.

`BUDGET_ENFORCE=false` (already set on the build step) only disables
a *different* plugin (`performanceBudgetPlugin`), not the SEO gate.

Fix
---
`.github/workflows/bundle-size-gate.yml`:
- Set `SEO_GATE_BYPASS: '1'` on the `Build project` step, with a long
  comment explaining the rationale alongside the existing
  `BUDGET_ENFORCE=false` note. This isolates the bundle-size workflow
  from SEO concerns, matching how Vercel already operates.
- Add a new `Verify build produced dist/assets` step that fails fast
  with a clear `::error::` annotation if a future plugin again kills
  the build silently — preventing recurrence of the cryptic
  "dist/assets not found" error from the gate script.

Verified locally
----------------
- `BUDGET_ENFORCE=false npx vite build` → fails on SEO gate (repro).
- `SEO_GATE_BYPASS=1 BUDGET_ENFORCE=false npx vite build` → ✓ built
  in 2m 12s, 2370 files in dist/assets.
- `BUNDLE_SIZE_THRESHOLD=0.10 BUNDLE_SIZE_BASELINE_REF=origin/main
  npm run bundle:gate` → exit 0 (placeholder baseline, comparison
  skipped as designed).

Out of scope (proposed as follow-ups)
-------------------------------------
- The 10,426 SEO description-length violations themselves (#959).
- Seeding the still-placeholder `bundle-size-baseline.json` so PRs are
  actually gated against real numbers (#960). The baseline will seed
  itself on the next push to main via the existing "Refresh baseline"
  step, which now reaches dist/assets successfully.

The +10% threshold (`BUNDLE_SIZE_THRESHOLD: '0.10'`) and all gate
logic are unchanged.

